@startuml resolve
' SPEC: _spec/apps/ui/starchess/resolve.puml
' OUTDATED: Phase 5–6 — live resolve in packages/starchess-core/src/resolve.
' purpose: Rank-major resolve — turn-open king-checks (before intent) → End: B → C → F.
!include ../../../themes/proveo.puml

title StarChess · Resolve — 3 phases: attack → move → fog approach

start

:Take planning snap — turn N is open;

:**Turn-open legal king-checks** (""beginScTurn"") — fog-visible, implicit,\nwhite then black (""applyPendingKingShots"").\nResolved **before** players choose intent. A unit that\nbreaks contact later this turn already paid a **parting shot**;\n

if (the two kings are adjacent?) then (yes)
  :**King duel** — a king is a legal checker of the enemy king.\nThe collector loops **both** king colours independently, so\ncontact is always **mutual**. Damage is **per checker**: every\nunit checking a king costs it 1 HP, so N checkers = N HP.\nKings leap (""leapsPiece"") → never the blocker / collision\nbranch: adjacency always chips, nothing is captured, the\nplacement is untouched;
else (no)
  :Only checkers with clear geometry to the king chip;
endif

if (either king at 0 HP after turn-open checks?) then (yes)
  :Phase **""O""** — no intent / B / C / F;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Players queue intent (specials + classical);

:End / timeout — ""endScTurn"" (live passes\n""skipTurnStartChecks"" when checks already applied);

:Apply rank **B** specials — white then black\n(spawn / mine / warp / siege);

:Rank **C** — classical for both sides against\nthe same start board (""resolveTurn"");

:Phase 1 **attack** — direct attacks on targets visible\nfrom the start board: attack → death → occupy;

if (attack hits a piece?) then (yes)
  :Death — victim removed;
  if (attacker survives?) then (yes)
    :**Occupy** victim's square;
  else (no)
    :Attacker dies first —\nsquare stays empty, no occupy;
  endif
else (no)
  :No direct hit —\nquiet intent defers to phase 2;
endif

:Phase 2 **move** — survivors relocate; collisions\nresolved against the post-attack board; a target\n**still fogged at contact** → move collision\n(capture/occupy, no attack cue);

:Phase 3 **fog approach** — path-reveal shots slide\n""pathRevealFrom"" → discovery square → attack;\n**King HP mid-resolve** only here: fog intent finds a\nhidden king on the path (""pathReveal"" kingShot).\nVisible kings already paid at turn open — no second chip.\n**fizzle unless** the attacker still occupies\n""pathRevealFrom"" (died in phases 1–2 / square\nre-occupied by a phase-2 mover / sieged — rooks\nnever relocate) and ""to"" holds the exact\nin-the-way victim (empty, converging ally, or a\ndifferent non-in-the-way enemy → fizzle, no capture);

:Apply rank **F** specials — white then black\n(post-move siege / late drops);

if (either king at 0 HP after all ranks?) then (yes)
  :Next snap phase **""O""** — terminal and **absorbing**\n(""endScTurn"" throws on a non-""P"" snapshot).\n""scOutcome(snap)"" derives the result from ""kingLives""\nalone: 0/0 → **draw**, one side at 0 → the other wins;
else (no)
  :Next snap phase **""P""** — play continues;
endif

note right
  **Promotion (after move/mine):** relocate lands a **pawn**; survivors with
  a queued promotion then **walk off** the board edge (1× ""MOVE_SQUARE_MS"")
  and the chosen unit **deploys**. A promoting pawn that **walks onto** a
  hostile mine (forward step — pawns only attack front diagonals) dies with
  the mine — **no** walk-off / deploy. Units that attack the mine square
  clear it in the attack phase then occupy.
  Completed-history wire ""C=from intentTo>resolvedTo"" remains **deferred**.
end note

stop

note right
  **Intent ""C="" vs progressive path resolve:** ""pathRevealSteps"" /
  ""pathRevealFrom"" in ""resolveTurn"" capture the fog approach — now a
  **phase-3** event: the attacker slides from ""pathRevealFrom"" to the
  discovery square, then attacks, applied **after** moves. An approach
  **fizzles** when the attacker no longer occupies ""pathRevealFrom""
  (died in phases 1–2, or its square was re-occupied by a phase-2 mover
  — ""destinationsWritten""), when the origin is sieged (""siegedRooks""
  — rooks never relocate), or when ""to"" no longer holds the exact
  in-the-way victim (""a.victim"" color+type): empty, a converging
  same-side ally, or a different enemy not in the way — never captured.
  Sieged rooks also **fizzle fogged contact** — they never relocate, so
  a fogged adjacent (or never-revealed) target and a fogged mine square
  are not attacked; visible targets still die to the turret.
  ""applyPathRevealAttack(snap, a)"" is the shared source of truth for the
  board-state fizzles (attacker still on ""pathRevealFrom"", exact victim on
  ""to""); the engine loop pre-filters the siege (""siegedRooks"") and
  origin-re-occupation (""destinationsWritten"") gates before the attack is
  listed, and the UI replay (""useStarChessCombat"" →
  ""playPathRevealAttacks"") replays only that fired list, so
  ""pathRevealAttacks"" holds **only attacks that fired**.
  ""resolveTurn"" returns ""attacks"" (phase 1),
  ""moves"" / ""mineTriggers"" / ""moveCollisions"" (phase 2),
  ""pathRevealAttacks"" (phase 3), and the snapshots ""afterMove""
  (post-phase-2) and ""afterAll"" (post-phase-3).
  **King shots:** ""collectLegalKingChecks"" + ""applyPendingKingShots""
  via ""beginScTurn"" at turn open (before intent). The **only** mid-resolve
  king HP is fog path-discovery (""applyPathRevealKingShot""): intent into
  fog finds a hidden king on the ray. Live ""endScTurn"" skips re-application
  of turn-open checks (""skipTurnStartChecks""); atomic replay may still run
  checks inside ""endScTurn"". No king-aimed ""C="".
  ====
  **King duel — two adjacent kings fight face-to-face.**
  ""collectLegalKingChecks"" does **not** exclude king-type attackers, so a
  king is a legal implicit checker of the enemy king. The collector loops
  both king colours independently, so contact is always **mutual**.
  Damage is **per checking unit**, not capped per turn: every unit that
  checks a king takes 1 HP off it, so N checkers cost N HP in one pass.
  A lone duel is therefore 1 HP each way at turn start.
  * **Kings leap** (""leapsPiece"" includes 'k'), so a duel never takes the
    blocker / collision branch: adjacency always chips, nothing is
    captured, the placement is returned untouched.
  * **Firing is never gated on the shooter's own HP** — only on board
    occupancy and target identity. A king reduced to 0 in the **same** pass
    still returns fire. Deliberate and load-bearing: it is what makes equal
    HP end 0/0 a **draw** instead of a win for whoever is ordered first
    (white sorts first). ""resolveTurn"" carries a comment warning against
    //fixing// it.
  * **Equal HP** drains 3/3 → 2/2 → 1/1 → 0/0 and flips phase to ""O""
    (a draw). **Unequal HP**: the lower king dies first.
  * **Deploy race** — a king deploys onto its own adjacent ring, so a unit
    spawned next to the enemy king stacks a **second** checker. Per-checker
    damage then chips **2 HP/turn** while taking 1. The doubling is an
    intended feature of the rule, and follows from the per-checker rule
    rather than being a special case.
  * **Parting shot** — pendings are computed before the move phase, so a
    king that breaks contact still loses 1 HP that turn.
  * **Immediate exit** — the moment a king is left at 0 HP the turn **bails
    out**: from the check phase nothing else resolves at all (no B, C or F),
    and from the classical pass no F special resolves behind the dead king
    (""endScTurn"" returns a terminal result at both seams). The classical
    pass is simultaneous, so it completes as one unit before the far-side
    bail out. Both shots of a duel are already applied, so mutual death
    still reads 0/0 = draw.
  * **Fog-discovered check** — the mid-path king chip is deliberately **not**
    fog-gated, unlike the turn-start check. A slider with no vision of the
    enemy king still chips it by walking its ray into it: that is a
    //discovered check//, which is a plain check once the fog is lifted, so
    the damage stands. The mover stops **before** the king (never occupies
    it), and such a killing blow bails the turn out like any other.
  Phase ""O"" is **absorbing** (""endScTurn"" throws on a non-""P"" snapshot),
  and ""parseScFen"" rejects a 0-HP side outside phase ""O"" so a dead king
  can never sit in a playable snapshot.
  ""scOutcome(snap)"" (""scOutcome.ts"") returns ""{winner:'w'}"" /
  ""{winner:'b'}"" for a win, ""{winner:null,draw:true}"" for a draw, or
  ""null"" while play continues — derived purely from
  ""kingLives"". HP is the single source of truth, so there is no
  persisted winner field and **no SCFEN grammar change**
  (""STARCHESS_FEN.md"" stays as is; ""O"" was already a valid phase code).
  Covered by core unit tests under ""packages/starchess-core""
  (historical path: ""src/starchess/__tests__/kingDuel.test.ts"").
end note
@enduml
